/*
    Here we test some bitwise operations. For example:
    `1 + 8 >> 2 + 1`

    First of all, in parser precedences table we set the right shift's operation as priority, so
    it must be evaluated first. Then program should get a sum of `1 + 1 + 1`. Calculations
    steps are written below:

    I.  1 + 8 >> 2 + 1
    II. 1 + (1000 >> 2) + 1
    III. 1 + 1 + 1 = 3
    
    Result: 3
*/

let x = 1 + 8 >> 2 + 1; // 3
let y = x | 5;          // 011 | 101

/* 3 | 5
    011
    101
    ---
    111
 Result: 7
*/ 

if (y == 7) {
    return "Correct!";
} else {
    return "Incorrect!";
}
